    <!-- Common Mistakes Section -->
    <section style="margin: 2.5rem 0;" aria-labelledby="mistakes-heading">
      <h2 id="mistakes-heading">Common Text Counting Discrepancies</h2>
      <ul style="color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.8; margin-left: 1.25rem;">
        <li><strong>Hyphenated Compound Words:</strong> Different word processors count hyphenated words differently (e.g., 'state-of-the-art'). Microsoft Word counts this as 4 words, while some older editors count it as 1. Our tool treats hyphenated components as individual lexical units.</li>
        <li><strong>Emoji Surrogate Pairs:</strong> JavaScript strings traditionally measure UTF-16 code units, causing emojis like 🚀 to count as 2 characters. Our Unicode-aware character counter normalizes surrogate pairs so each visible emoji counts as 1 character.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
